0347-negroni-awdl: AirDrop AWDL engine (boot-arg negroniawdl, default on; kill switch negroniawdl=0; docs/airdrop-plan.md).
In-kernel AWDL (Apple Wireless Direct Link) on the WCN6855 Wi-Fi driver, a port of seemoo-lab/owl (GPL-3.0-or-later, pin
0ee3263f944ea721c355f826aa90d636d012a512): negroni_awdl_owl.c/.h hold the ported sync math, election and frame build/parse;
negroni_awdl.c holds the engine on the Wi-Fi driver thread (from negroni_wlan_sta_service). It parks on channel 6 by a
single-channel passive scan with the offchan-mgmt-tx flag and its own scan id (en0's scan id is untouched), runs only while
en0 is idle, and gives the radio back (STOP_SCAN) the moment en0 needs it. PSF every 110 TU and MIF are sent by
WMI_MGMT_TX_SEND from our own DMA slots (desc ids 0x100+); a TX-completion hook clears the slots. RX AWDL action frames go
to the OWL receive code (peer table, election). Self-checks (NO PROBES rule): no WMI_SERVICE_MGMT_TX_WMI (76) turns the
engine off with one line; failed TX completions turn it off with the status; awdl0 and the AirLink IOService are made ONLY
after the first received AWDL frame proves the firmware passes AWDL frames to the host. wifip2pd's AWDL_SYNC_ENABLED is
answered; the other APPLE80211_IOC_AWDL_* requests are logged and get a clean error (the work list, step 6). Bit 0 (RX
classification) and bit 1 (awdl0 observer) are the earlier probe, kept. Details: patches/xnu/README-wifi.md "0347".
Review fixes (2026-10-27): negroni_awdl_yield() stops our ROC scan and waits <= 300 ms for its end before en0's
scan and before a join/disassociate; STOP_SCAN req_type WMI_SCAN_STOP_ONE = 0; one ROC at a time (no re-arm before
the end event), back-off + engine off after 10 failed ROC starts; TX only while our ROC runs; lost TX completions
free the slot after 1 s, 8 lost with none completed = engine off; awdl0 with the engine bit waits for RX + one TX OK;
the RX path runs for every non-zero negroniawdl (bits 2/4 alone work) and only after negroni_awdl_start.

